{
  "about": "Git capture (spec 2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design §9.1, §9.2) of fixed repository states. The Rust capture (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx_capture_tests.rs) and the Pi extension's (plugins/pi/test/git.test.ts) both build each case and must report `expect` exactly. Each case starts in an empty directory: `mkdir` makes a directory, `write` writes `text` as UTF-8, `remove` deletes a file, and `git` runs git in the directory `in` (the case's own when absent) with `fixture.config` as -c options and `fixture.env` set. The capture runs in `cwd`. `expect` is the context without `captured_at`, its `repo_root` relative to the case's directory, or {\"git_capture\": outcome}.",
